WEBVTT

00:00:07.690 --> 00:00:12.320
We had a nice haul at the morning market today, huh, Hakumei?

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:13.860
We bought too much.

00:00:14.410 --> 00:00:18.490
I just want to go back home and keep working.

00:00:18.910 --> 00:00:21.870
What are you working on, anyway?

00:00:22.580 --> 00:00:27.380
Oh, Sen shared some quality gunpowder with me.

00:00:36.430 --> 00:00:38.930
So I'm going to make firew—

00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:40.890
Hakumei!

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:29.290
Yep, that's a lens fire.

00:02:30.460 --> 00:02:36.800
Put simply, that's when something like a glass marble or a vase acts as a lens and sparks a fire.

00:02:37.260 --> 00:02:41.300
So you have to be careful not to leave things like that around the window,

00:02:41.970 --> 00:02:46.060
especially if you're dealing with gunpowder.

00:02:47.140 --> 00:02:49.690
It's a bit late for that.

00:02:49.690 --> 00:02:50.690
Sure is.

00:02:51.650 --> 00:02:52.730
Yeah.

00:02:53.900 --> 00:02:56.070
Well, leave the repairs to me.

00:02:58.570 --> 00:03:01.780
I brought a crack team of heavy lifters along with me.

00:03:01.780 --> 00:03:03.200
That's big...

00:03:13.080 --> 00:03:18.050
We'll finish in around a day, so is there somewhere you can stay the night?

00:03:18.670 --> 00:03:24.100
Hmm, where will we stay?
Konju's place is apparently pretty small.

00:03:24.100 --> 00:03:27.060
Hey, Mikochi!

00:03:27.810 --> 00:03:29.480
Let's get going!

00:03:30.980 --> 00:03:32.350
We're going camping!

00:03:33.060 --> 00:03:35.270
Camping?!

00:03:41.780 --> 00:03:44.530
Now, where should we set up?

00:03:45.160 --> 00:03:48.580
Why are we going camping, anyway?

00:03:50.620 --> 00:03:53.580
I did it a lot back when I was homeless.

00:03:55.210 --> 00:03:56.840
It's fun!

00:03:59.590 --> 00:04:02.470
I like having a roof over my head.

00:04:05.050 --> 00:04:07.470
Perfect. A ponkan tree.

00:04:11.730 --> 00:04:12.440
Hup.

00:04:13.600 --> 00:04:15.520
We'll set up camp right here.

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:18.570
Why below a ponkan tree?

00:04:18.940 --> 00:04:24.610
Citrus trees have dense leaf coverage that's close to the ground. It'll protect us from wind and rain.

00:04:26.700 --> 00:04:30.240
Now that we've picked a spot, we ought to...

00:04:32.460 --> 00:04:35.040
This ponkan is delicious.

00:04:43.720 --> 00:04:47.180
You mind if we grab a few of those persimmon leaves?

00:04:47.180 --> 00:04:50.220
Sure. How about this one?

00:04:50.220 --> 00:04:51.850
You've already eaten it!

00:04:55.900 --> 00:04:58.110
What are the persimmon leaves for?

00:04:58.980 --> 00:05:00.190
We're making a tent.

00:05:01.070 --> 00:05:04.700
Cut holes along the marks I'm making.

00:05:04.700 --> 00:05:05.450
Okay.

00:05:10.450 --> 00:05:14.460
Then we'll pass a bristle grass stem through the holes.

00:05:14.910 --> 00:05:16.080
And stand it up!

00:05:19.590 --> 00:05:21.880
Wow, it's a tent!

00:05:23.300 --> 00:05:25.720
Tie some key points up with a rope,

00:05:25.720 --> 00:05:30.510
and secure the excess rope to a stone outside to anchor it.

00:05:31.010 --> 00:05:33.100
Should I do the other side?

00:05:33.100 --> 00:05:37.600
Nah, I'll take care of it.
It takes some muscle to get it done.

00:05:38.100 --> 00:05:39.900
You can handle this instead.

00:05:39.900 --> 00:05:40.730
All yours!

00:05:42.230 --> 00:05:43.940
Wild onion roots?

00:05:44.440 --> 00:05:46.360
I found them earlier.

00:05:47.200 --> 00:05:51.870
Use it in our dinner. Like in a whole roast or a parchment roast...

00:05:51.870 --> 00:05:54.370
Aren't those practically the same?

00:06:02.250 --> 00:06:06.510
Ah, jeez! I go to draw one bucket of water and this happens?

00:06:10.640 --> 00:06:17.140
And there's no kitchen... How will I start a fire?

00:06:17.520 --> 00:06:19.440
Hey, Mikochi.

00:06:21.270 --> 00:06:23.690
I set up a Dutch oven and stuff.

00:06:26.030 --> 00:06:27.900
As for firewood...

00:06:29.410 --> 00:06:31.780
Huh? Mikochi?

00:06:40.540 --> 00:06:42.790
Okay, this should do it.

00:06:43.460 --> 00:06:47.050
Hey, Mikochi, how's it going over there?

00:06:50.680 --> 00:06:53.050
Quite a fire you've got going.

00:06:53.510 --> 00:06:58.180
With all this wood lying around, I guess I got carried away...

00:07:04.190 --> 00:07:06.150
Persimmon leaf tea, huh?

00:07:06.150 --> 00:07:09.030
The grassy flavor's a little strong, but it's delicious.

00:07:09.030 --> 00:07:11.320
That's because I hadn't steamed it.

00:07:13.320 --> 00:07:20.580
First, mince the wild onion, and add our supply of dried meat, pine nuts, and ostrich fern buds to the shiitake mushrooms.

00:07:20.580 --> 00:07:22.380
Hakumei, you help too.

00:07:27.170 --> 00:07:29.300
That about does it for the soup.

00:07:30.010 --> 00:07:31.880
Did you crush the rice?

00:07:31.880 --> 00:07:34.180
This is really hard work!

00:07:36.220 --> 00:07:40.600
Yeah, this is probably enough. Thanks.

00:07:40.600 --> 00:07:42.560
I'm starving.

00:07:42.900 --> 00:07:45.940
Just sit right there and leave the rest to me!

00:07:45.940 --> 00:07:47.730
It'll be ready in about an hour!

00:07:47.730 --> 00:07:49.070
One hour...

00:07:56.280 --> 00:07:58.040
Amazing!

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:01.500
Derishish!

00:08:01.500 --> 00:08:04.290
That's the wild vegetable and dried meat risotto.

00:08:04.790 --> 00:08:07.840
Even out here, I can still make some decent food.

00:08:08.630 --> 00:08:12.090
Your cooking is delicious no matter where we are, Mikochi.

00:08:12.090 --> 00:08:15.590
Oh hey, I have whole roast and a parchment roast, too.

00:08:16.760 --> 00:08:18.680
Haven't you made too much?

00:08:20.850 --> 00:08:22.440
You'll eat it, right?

00:08:36.280 --> 00:08:38.530
I can't eat another bite.

00:08:39.700 --> 00:08:43.160
Sorry. Turns out I did make too much.

00:08:45.120 --> 00:08:48.590
Camping sure is nice, isn't it?

00:08:48.590 --> 00:08:50.130
I guess so.

00:08:50.550 --> 00:08:52.720
Tents have roofs too, I suppose.

00:08:57.550 --> 00:08:59.350
Hold still a sec!

00:08:59.760 --> 00:09:00.770
What?!

00:09:01.140 --> 00:09:02.810
Don't drag me!

00:09:02.810 --> 00:09:04.770
What's inside will come out...

00:09:29.710 --> 00:09:32.550
<i>This</i> is our roof. All of it.

00:09:36.760 --> 00:09:38.050
I see.

00:09:38.510 --> 00:09:40.390
It does have a certain charm about it.

00:09:40.970 --> 00:09:41.890
Doesn't it?

00:10:01.700 --> 00:10:03.830
Oh, welcome back.

00:10:05.160 --> 00:10:07.330
We're home...

00:10:08.960 --> 00:10:11.460
We brought you a gift.

00:10:11.460 --> 00:10:15.920
It has a nice citrus fragrance...
Or is it your bodies I smell?

00:10:15.920 --> 00:10:18.590
We drank in a bit too much of the outdoors.

00:10:19.590 --> 00:10:23.600
Well, I've finished the repairs, so will you give the inside a look?

00:10:23.600 --> 00:10:26.390
Yeah! You work as fast as expected!

00:10:26.390 --> 00:10:28.270
Thank you, Sen.

00:10:31.360 --> 00:10:35.360
The entranceway is reserved for last,
so we'll go in through the back.

00:10:39.490 --> 00:10:43.280
I simply used the tree hollow for the inside part.

00:10:43.280 --> 00:10:45.620
It'll be quite sturdy now.

00:10:46.910 --> 00:10:48.910
This looks good.

00:10:48.910 --> 00:10:51.880
It's like the place I used to live a long time ago.

00:10:52.540 --> 00:10:54.670
Is there a room back there, too?

00:10:54.670 --> 00:10:55.750
Yes.

00:10:56.710 --> 00:11:02.050
There was an empty space between the roots, so I just had to make one.

00:11:06.020 --> 00:11:10.100
It's a glass greenhouse—<i>and</i> a laboratory!

00:11:11.730 --> 00:11:13.650
Laboratory?

00:11:13.650 --> 00:11:15.400
I thought you would need it!

00:11:17.070 --> 00:11:20.030
And now, the crown jewel of my work—the entryway.

00:11:20.030 --> 00:11:21.240
To the front.

00:11:21.240 --> 00:11:22.410
I kind of...

00:11:22.410 --> 00:11:24.780
...have a bad feeling about this.

00:11:25.990 --> 00:11:27.160
The entryway!

00:11:27.160 --> 00:11:31.460
I attempted a daring use of the rib cage! Very cool, is it not?

00:11:36.670 --> 00:11:39.420
Um... Thanks.

00:11:44.300 --> 00:11:45.050
<i>But...</i>

00:11:46.430 --> 00:11:49.060
<i>It was surprisingly cozy.</i>

00:12:04.780 --> 00:12:05.740
Excuse me.

00:12:13.370 --> 00:12:16.210
Who the hell are you, runt?

00:12:16.210 --> 00:12:19.300
I'm Hakumei. I started working here today.

00:12:19.300 --> 00:12:21.090
Nice to meet you, old timer.

00:12:21.090 --> 00:12:24.340
Ah, so you're the helper that I've been hearin' about?

00:12:24.340 --> 00:12:28.310
Can a runt like you really do carpentry?

00:12:31.520 --> 00:12:36.480
I already repaired the rain gutter and replaced some bricks on the other side.

00:12:36.860 --> 00:12:38.480
Was that okay?

00:12:39.730 --> 00:12:41.440
Well yeah, that's fine.

00:12:42.110 --> 00:12:46.070
Then since I'm going to help you over here, I need to change real quick.

00:12:46.070 --> 00:12:46.990
Okay.

00:12:48.580 --> 00:12:51.370
I'm the boss out here. Name's Iwashidani.

00:12:51.750 --> 00:12:54.040
You're a weasel, but you're named sardine?
iwashi
itachi

00:12:54.620 --> 00:12:55.920
Shuddup.

00:13:04.300 --> 00:13:07.340
Newspaper fee collection!

00:13:07.340 --> 00:13:08.640
Coming!

00:13:11.640 --> 00:13:14.440
Good morning, Hakumei-san.

00:13:14.440 --> 00:13:16.650
Oh, hi.

00:13:19.110 --> 00:13:21.320
I apologize for keeping you waiting.

00:13:21.320 --> 00:13:22.530
Oh, it's fine.

00:13:23.150 --> 00:13:26.660
Mikochi-san, I have an awkward question, but...

00:13:26.660 --> 00:13:27.700
Yes?

00:13:27.700 --> 00:13:30.580
Did you have a fight with
Hakumei-san or something?

00:13:31.790 --> 00:13:35.080
Well... She seemed to be in a bad mood.

00:13:35.080 --> 00:13:39.880
Oh, that's just her killer stare.
She's in work mode.

00:13:40.250 --> 00:13:42.630
What kind of job does she do?

00:13:42.630 --> 00:13:44.300
She does repairs.

00:13:44.300 --> 00:13:47.720
From sharpening knives to doing windmill maintenance.

00:13:58.190 --> 00:14:00.270
Morning, Iwashi!

00:14:01.940 --> 00:14:06.860
How many times do I gotta tell ya?
It's boss Iwashidani to you!

00:14:06.860 --> 00:14:08.660
Now, now...

00:14:10.160 --> 00:14:13.790
For a "boss," you sure haven't taught me anything.

00:14:13.790 --> 00:14:15.910
I'm not an instructor.

00:14:15.910 --> 00:14:17.410
You don't have any underlings, either.

00:14:17.410 --> 00:14:19.290
Then what the hell are <i>you</i>?!

00:14:19.670 --> 00:14:22.210
So. What are we looking at here?

00:14:22.210 --> 00:14:23.550
Hm?

00:14:23.550 --> 00:14:27.420
Today's going to be a tricky one. A brake wheel.

00:14:27.420 --> 00:14:29.180
It's the cog at the very top.

00:14:29.180 --> 00:14:29.930
Oh.

00:14:31.680 --> 00:14:36.020
Looks like one of the teeth is damaged. It's fixin' to break completely.

00:14:36.020 --> 00:14:40.810
Gotta clean that up, put in a new tooth, and we're done.

00:14:41.190 --> 00:14:46.690
But you know how cramped and steep that tower is. And the cog's so damn high.

00:14:49.990 --> 00:14:53.700
Since it's dangerous, I'd like to take apart the roof and deal with it myself,

00:14:54.410 --> 00:14:57.700
But there's rain in the forecast for tonight.

00:14:59.790 --> 00:15:04.170
Hakumei, I won't make you, but could you go in—

00:15:04.170 --> 00:15:06.210
You're all ready?!

00:15:07.130 --> 00:15:08.510
You gonna be okay?

00:15:08.510 --> 00:15:10.340
I'll make it work.

00:15:10.880 --> 00:15:13.470
Let's start by laying a platform to stand on.

00:15:16.770 --> 00:15:18.230
Hey.

00:15:18.520 --> 00:15:20.560
I removed all the sailcloth.

00:15:20.980 --> 00:15:22.270
Okay.

00:15:23.270 --> 00:15:27.070
Iwashi. Can you come to the roof for a sec?

00:15:29.990 --> 00:15:31.410
What do you need?

00:15:31.410 --> 00:15:35.330
I'm gonna throw the rope, so keep clear!

00:15:35.330 --> 00:15:36.120
There!

00:15:36.660 --> 00:15:38.370
Okay, it's out.

00:15:38.790 --> 00:15:42.580
I want to lift this beam, but it's a big one. Can you pull it up?

00:15:42.580 --> 00:15:44.630
No problem. I got it handled.

00:15:45.710 --> 00:15:47.880
Heave!

00:15:48.880 --> 00:15:50.260
That was fast!

00:15:50.720 --> 00:15:53.050
Thanks, Iwashi!

00:15:53.050 --> 00:15:55.260
No... No problem!

00:15:56.850 --> 00:15:59.770
The platform's done, so I'm going to start on the cog.

00:16:00.810 --> 00:16:02.640
Careful in there.

00:16:02.640 --> 00:16:03.770
Okay.

00:16:04.690 --> 00:16:07.520
If I take a fall, I'll ring the bell, okay?

00:16:07.520 --> 00:16:10.530
Even if it rings, what the hell am <i>I</i> gonna do?

00:16:12.030 --> 00:16:13.740
H-Hey!

00:16:16.990 --> 00:16:20.500
You haven't eaten lunch yet, right? Want some?

00:16:20.500 --> 00:16:22.040
Quit messin' around!

00:16:26.000 --> 00:16:28.000
How's it coming?

00:16:28.420 --> 00:16:30.550
Getting there, I think.

00:16:31.510 --> 00:16:34.340
No, no... I mean your repair business.

00:16:34.340 --> 00:16:35.300
Oh...

00:16:36.140 --> 00:16:38.640
I fixed a dresser a little while ago.

00:16:38.640 --> 00:16:40.140
Whose?

00:16:40.140 --> 00:16:41.310
Mine.

00:16:43.230 --> 00:16:45.350
Business isn't exactly booming, huh?

00:16:45.350 --> 00:16:46.690
Leave me alone.

00:16:46.690 --> 00:16:50.440
Well, I guess Mikochi's got a good job, so you'll probably be fine.

00:16:50.940 --> 00:16:53.450
Yeah, <i>that's</i> a responsible way to think.

00:16:53.450 --> 00:16:56.780
I'm out of work 'cause I repair everything too well.

00:16:56.780 --> 00:16:58.580
Ha! No doubt!

00:16:59.330 --> 00:17:03.120
By the way, Iwashi,
Mikochi said something to me earlier.

00:17:03.960 --> 00:17:07.540
Do you think I have a killer stare while I'm working?

00:17:10.880 --> 00:17:12.460
Hey, quit it.

00:17:12.840 --> 00:17:15.380
More than normal, I s'pose.

00:17:16.720 --> 00:17:17.930
I see.

00:17:27.400 --> 00:17:29.940
The clouds look like they're ready to ruin our day.

00:17:29.940 --> 00:17:31.900
I'll hurry it up and finish.

00:17:33.990 --> 00:17:36.530
Making a tooth isn't easy, you know.

00:17:36.530 --> 00:17:39.030
If the measurements are even a smidgen off...

00:17:39.570 --> 00:17:40.870
How's this?

00:17:40.870 --> 00:17:42.490
You're done already?!

00:17:45.620 --> 00:17:49.580
I'm not sure how <i>you</i> manage to do work this good.

00:17:49.580 --> 00:17:50.880
I know, right?

00:18:04.850 --> 00:18:06.890
Repairs are done.

00:18:07.440 --> 00:18:08.810
I'm finished!

00:18:08.810 --> 00:18:12.650
Good job! Looks like this is about to turn into a storm!

00:18:12.650 --> 00:18:15.030
And... there.

00:18:25.410 --> 00:18:27.870
Hakumei! What happened?!

00:18:30.710 --> 00:18:33.050
Sorry! I screwed up!

00:18:33.300 --> 00:18:34.590
What about the platform?

00:18:34.590 --> 00:18:35.920
It collapsed!

00:18:35.920 --> 00:18:38.930
I'm hanging on... to the bell cord, but...

00:18:42.850 --> 00:18:43.930
Ah, crud!

00:18:51.650 --> 00:18:52.940
Boss!

00:19:04.370 --> 00:19:05.830
Boss?

00:19:05.830 --> 00:19:08.160
You all right, Hakumei?

00:19:09.040 --> 00:19:11.790
Y-Yeah.

00:19:16.300 --> 00:19:18.760
We broke the window.

00:19:21.050 --> 00:19:23.550
Well, guess we'll fix it tomorrow.

00:19:26.850 --> 00:19:27.970
Your sandal...

00:19:28.810 --> 00:19:30.060
Huh?

00:19:30.060 --> 00:19:33.110
Oh, the strap broke?

00:19:33.940 --> 00:19:34.980
Ah, well.

00:19:36.070 --> 00:19:37.320
Boss...

00:19:37.320 --> 00:19:38.320
Hmm?

00:19:39.690 --> 00:19:40.950
I'm sorry.

00:19:49.410 --> 00:19:53.960
Fix that for me. I'll add it to your pay tomorrow.

00:19:54.670 --> 00:19:57.170
Boss, I can't accept pay f—

00:19:57.170 --> 00:19:59.710
Stop calling me that.

00:20:00.470 --> 00:20:02.340
Hurry on home.

00:20:22.950 --> 00:20:25.070
Was the rope too slack?

00:20:26.120 --> 00:20:30.790
Extra material for sandals... I'm sure Mikochi has some.

00:20:51.390 --> 00:20:53.060
I'm home—

00:20:53.770 --> 00:20:56.480
Wel-come BACK!

00:21:00.110 --> 00:21:03.030
I won't blame you for forgetting an umbrella,

00:21:03.030 --> 00:21:05.530
but at least try to run home!

00:21:05.530 --> 00:21:07.620
What will you do if you catch cold?!

00:21:08.200 --> 00:21:09.780
Sorry.

00:21:12.160 --> 00:21:13.500
What's that?

00:21:14.040 --> 00:21:15.290
A sandal.

00:21:16.000 --> 00:21:17.500
I'm gonna fix it now.

00:21:19.460 --> 00:21:21.050
Before that...

00:21:21.420 --> 00:21:23.470
Get yourself into the bath!

00:21:23.470 --> 00:21:25.800
Uh... Wait!

00:21:29.550 --> 00:21:33.020
Mikochi, do you have anything to repair—

00:21:33.020 --> 00:21:34.770
Do I have to wash you myself?!

00:21:35.810 --> 00:21:37.980
Get in up to your shoulders.

00:21:37.980 --> 00:21:39.020
Okay.

00:21:45.070 --> 00:21:45.950
Here.

00:21:46.660 --> 00:21:48.320
Hm? This scent...

00:21:48.820 --> 00:21:51.580
I made some jam from that ponkan and put it in the tea.

00:21:52.040 --> 00:21:53.540
It'll warm you up.

00:21:57.370 --> 00:21:59.080
Want me to help you with that?

00:21:59.080 --> 00:22:02.630
Hmm? Oh, nah, I'm done.

00:22:04.970 --> 00:22:06.050
Thanks, though.

00:22:07.050 --> 00:22:08.050
Good to hear.

00:22:27.450 --> 00:22:35.540
When the breeze is pleasant, let's eat outside

00:22:35.540 --> 00:22:43.340
The olives are fragrant this time of year

00:22:43.340 --> 00:22:47.340
And in the plum-colored sky,

00:22:47.340 --> 00:22:51.300
the stars twinkle and shine

00:22:51.300 --> 00:22:55.850
After we take in an easy breath,

00:22:55.850 --> 00:23:00.230
the banquet will begin!

00:23:00.230 --> 00:23:03.820
A freshly-made smoked cheese quiche,

00:23:03.820 --> 00:23:07.570
sockeye salmon wrapped in magnolia leaves

00:23:07.570 --> 00:23:11.490
Look, the whole world is rejoicing

00:23:11.490 --> 00:23:16.330
It's itching to dance with us

00:23:16.330 --> 00:23:20.290
And what drink might fit a night like this?

00:23:20.290 --> 00:23:24.250
How about something botanical with pepper in it?

00:23:24.250 --> 00:23:29.550
We could even catch the moon with our tiny hands

00:23:29.550 --> 00:23:33.090
At least, that's how we're feeling
